> Dear Mr. Condores P=C3=A9rez,
>
> Dear DGAC team,
>
> Thank you for your clarification regarding the submission process. I
> understand that all documentation must be sent as a single compressed fil=
e
> via the official Registratura channel to ensure proper processing and
> assignment of an expediente number.
>
> As requested, I have compiled the full documentation into a single .zip
> file, which is attached to this email. This file contains the (not yet)
> complete set of materials related to the incident involving LATAM flight
> LA8159 on July 5=E2=80=936, 2024, including:
>
>    -
>
>    A comprehensive master document detailing the chronology, evidence,
>    and analysis of the incident
>    -
>
>    Individual narrative summaries of each recorded interaction
>    -
>
>    Supporting transcripts, email chains, and related documentation
>
> Due to the volume of data (the file is over 1giga), I have also provided =
a
> secure download link below for your convenience, should you encounter any
> issues with the attachment:
>
> https://drive.google.com/file/d/1289W13XYDOvUKUxgaKf97ARJkmnqm6yJ
>
> Please note that the documentation is still being refined and
> cross-referenced. Additional information may follow as the analysis
> progresses. I believe it is in the DGAC=E2=80=99s interest to review this=
 material
> thoroughly, as it highlights serious procedural and regulatory concerns
> involving LATAM Airlines and multiple airport authorities.
>
> I would also like to reiterate the key question from my initial
> communication:
>
>  What procedures does the DGAC intend to initiate based on the
> documentation provided, and what is your official position regarding the
> events described?
>
> I expect formal acknowledgment of receipt and a clear response regarding
> the DGAC=E2=80=99s intended actions. This is not merely a passenger compl=
aint but a
> documented case involving potential violations of Chilean aviation law,
> passenger rights, and international standards.
>
> Thank you for your attention to this matter. I look forward to your timel=
y
> and substantive reply.
>
> Kind regards,
> Leandro Disconzi
